{"kind":"table","sheet":"SPPR diagnostics","address":"A1:J29","rows":29,"cols":10,"values":[["SPPR diagnostics: repaired source loader",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["ICES_WGSAM2015_North_Sea_1991 | Official rerun: 14 November 2026 | Raw SPPR coefficients below; no /9 carbon conversion. Taxon-mapping PPR in the first sheet remains in tonnes C.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["All three methods completed with WARN: no negative coefficients; 350 finite values per method (70 recipient groups × 5 basal sources). PP budgets close on the effective runtime. Numerical convergence is not researcher approval.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Configuration: EE floor ON, floor = 0.1, threshold = 0.1; diet normalization, GS defaults, zero catch, zero BA and BA reconciliation OFF. Detritus collapse = never; closed boundary (open mode none; theta = 1; external SPPR = 0).",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Repaired loader preserves source producer/detritus routing, TL, catch and known BA; accounts for documented fleet discard returns once. Four missing nonfeeding synthetic-import diet cells become structural runtime zeros; canonical source missingness is retained.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Named detritus coefficients are PP units per unit detritus. Negative source count covers all five source columns; negative entry count covers the full 70 × 5 matrix. Zero below is an observed count, not a substituted coefficient.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Method (engine ID)","Overall status","Living spectral radius (ρ)","Detritus coupling (b)","DetritusDOMWaterColumn (67) raw SPPR","DetritusPOMSediment (68) raw SPPR","Discards (69) raw SPPR","Negative entries","Negative sources","Finite matrix values"],["new_GE","WARN",0.2894427191062622,0.8822051250081107,3.462493358284118,5.344873625432921,440.27445855458177,0,0,350],["new_TE_EEfix","WARN",0.5734463993696682,0.1554967742366123,0.4294643281019556,0.4430838363796164,816.3858058146532,0,0,350],["new_WithEgestion","WARN",0.22945022049471692,0.9151607499042561,5.580806053974749,7.112556342678172,182.03671954514908,0,0,350],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Negative-entry ledger: empty for GE, TE and With Egestion (strict test < 0; tolerance 0). For every method, DetritusDOMWaterColumn (67), DetritusPOMSediment (68) and Discards (69) each have 0 negative entries. No negative-pair rows are omitted.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Warnings retained from the diagnostics",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["new_GE: diet rows deviate from 1 by up to 8.33e-05 (> 1e-06; ModelData.validate_DC only guards 1e-3) | b=0.8822 is within 0.3 of divergence (max sppr_det 440 PP-units per unit detritus) | max sppr_det=440 >= 10: converged, but detritus is implausibly expensive",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["new_TE_EEfix: diet rows deviate from 1 by up to 8.33e-05 (> 1e-06; ModelData.validate_DC only guards 1e-3) | max sppr_det=816 >= 10: converged, but detritus is implausibly expensive | 5 group(s) have near-zero TE (SPPR ~ 1/te is near-singular): [65, 4, 3, 2, 1]",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["new_WithEgestion: diet rows deviate from 1 by up to 8.33e-05 (> 1e-06; ModelData.validate_DC only guards 1e-3) | b=0.9152 is within 0.3 of divergence (max sppr_det 182 PP-units per unit detritus) | max sppr_det=182 >= 10: converged, but detritus is implausibly expensive",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Primary-production budget in the effective runtime (raw model PP currency; no carbon conversion)",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Method",null,"PP inflow",null,"PP outflow",null,"Relative gap (fraction)",null,"Balance status",null],["new_GE",null,2150.010358224,null,2150.0103582242664,null,1.239444947788965e-13,null,"OK",null],["new_TE_EEfix",null,2150.010358224,null,2150.0103582240986,null,4.589753475600775e-14,null,"OK",null],["new_WithEgestion",null,2150.010358224,null,2150.0103582241113,null,5.1819797305170045e-14,null,"OK",null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Source versus effective state: source detritus BA = 0 is retained before the EE floor. Positive effective detritus BA is the floor-runtime stock closure under the operational detritus EE = 1 convention; it is not observed author BA or an invented source export. Native equivalence remains unestablished.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["The EE-floor mortality sink is a calculation assumption (total 1.983704066273114 in model flow currency). TE now includes returned-catch coupling (b = 0.1554967742366123); the former b = 0 convention does not describe this run. Source catch and canonical inputs remain unchanged.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null],["Diagnostic summary and interpretation",null,null,null,null,"Complete negative-entry ledger (header only)",null,null,null,null],["Source / pre-floor / effective accounting review",null,null,null,null,"Full-precision official method diagnostics",null,null,null,null],["Source-loader preservation audit",null,null,null,null,"Official run manifest and evidence provenance",null,null,null,null]]}
